-- title:
--   (p) is radical on affine opens of X_O
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $O$ be a commutative ring in which the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$ is maximal. Write $\mathfrak{X} =$ `DRModel p` for the two-chart integral model over $\mathbb{Z}$ attached to the field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` and the element `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, namely the pushout of the two maps glueing the spectra of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebras generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$, and let `DRModel.toBase p : 𝔛 ⟶ Spec ℤ` be the morphism obtained from the structure maps of those two chart algebras. Form the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure morphism $\mathbb{Z} \to O$, and let $U$ be an affine open of this fibre product $\mathfrak{X}_O$. The assertion is that the ideal generated by the image of the natural number $p$ in the ring of sections $\Gamma(\mathfrak{X}_O, U)$ is a radical ideal, equivalently that $\Gamma(\mathfrak{X}_O,U)/(p)$ has no nonzero nilpotents. No further hypothesis is placed on $O$: in particular it need not be a domain or local ring, only $(p) \subset O$ maximal is required.
--
--   This is the local form, over an arbitrary base $O$ with $(p)$ maximal, of the classical statement that the special fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model is reduced (its two rational components meeting transversally at the supersingular points). It records the reducedness of the divisor $V(p) \subset \mathfrak{X}_O$ in the form needed when the properties of the Deligne–Rapoport model package are assembled and used further on.
